{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T04:47:49.708Z","ordinal":37748,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a10f8a-13cc-7811-859b-61ec23797216","call_id":"call_4FHJNpvRR0JRdJKP9IYlIvCG","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"a3a380\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":3945,\"output\":\"import { Effect, Schema } from \\\"effect\\\";\\n\\n/**\\n * A domain error raised when a tax calculation cannot be completed.\\n *\\n * @since 0.1.0\\n */\\nexport class CalculationError extends Schema.TaggedError<CalculationError>()(\\n  \\\"CalculationError\\\",\\n  {\\n    // Legacy diagnostic data remains opaque; its codec preserves key identity.\\n    cause: Schema.OptionFromOptionalKey(\\n      Schema.OptionFromUndefinedOr(Schema.Unknown)\\n    ).pipe(Schema.withConstructorDefault(Effect.succeedNone)),\\n    message: Schema.String,\\n  }\\n) {}\\n---\\ndocument_type: documentation-router\\nlifecycle: current\\nauthority: canonical\\nowner: taxkit-documentation-owner\\nlast_reviewed: 2026-07-24\\nreview_trigger: any maintainer/public docs class, root route, SPEC, plan, runbook, proof, evidence, or lifecycle change\\n---\\n\\n# TaxKit documentation\\n\\nThis is the sole router for maintainer-document type, lifecycle, truth layers,\\nand semantic ownership. Root `README.md` is the public repository entry point;\\n`AGENTS.md` is the short task map; `docs/architecture/README.md` is the current\\narchitecture route. Public documentation content is a separate product surface\\nowned by `apps/docs` and the docs packages.\\n\\n## Truth layers\\n\\nUse the strongest applicable owner and link rather than copy:\\n\\n1. External systems own their current external state at readback time.\\n2. Code, configuration, Schemas, package exports, workflows, and generated\\n   sources own desired/executable state.\\n3. Architecture and standards own durable boundaries and enforceable policy.\\n4. Dated proof/evidence owns one artifact/environment/authority observation and\\n   its limitations.\\n5. Active SPEC/tasks and execution plans own current implementation intent.\\n\\nProvider/registry output cannot grant authority. Completed plans are history.\\nLocal release checks do not prove npm publication or external consumers.\\n\\n## Metadata and lifecycle\\n\\nNew or materially revised maintainer docs separate `document_type`,\\n`lifecycle`, `authority`, and `owner`. Current durable docs also record\\n`last_reviewed` and `review_trigger`; superseded/tombstone docs record a\\nsuccessor and reason.\\n\\nLifecycle values are `proposed`, `current`, `implemented`, `superseded`,\\n`historical`, `evidence`, `reference`, `failed`, `inconclusive`, `tombstone`,\\nand `archived`. Authority values are `canonical`, `supporting`, `generated`,\\nand `external`. Legacy `status: canonical` is an authority marker, not a\\nlifecycle; migrate it only when its owner is materially revised.\\n\\n## Routes\\n\\n| Need | Owner | Use |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Architecture | [`architecture/README.md`](architecture/README.md) | Current architecture route. `architecture.md` is a tombstone only. |\\n| Standards | [`standards/README.md`](standards/README.md) | Current durable engineering/documentation rules. |\\n| Current intent | [`product-specs/index.md`](product-specs/index.md) and [`exec-plans/active/README.md`](exec-plans/active/README.md) | Only genuinely active work; implemented/history stays inventory. |\\n| Completed history | [`exec-plans/completed/README.md`](exec-plans/completed/README.md) | Historical provenance, never default policy. |\\n| Public docs product | [`../apps/docs/README.md`](../apps/docs/README.md), [`../packages/docs-content/README.md`](../packages/docs-content/README.md), and [`../packages/docs-fumadocs/README.md`](../packages/docs-fumadocs/README.md) | Consumer-facing content/runtime, not maintainer lifecycle policy. |\\n| Repeatable release/deployment/recovery operations | [`runbooks/README.md`](runbooks/README.md) and [`operations/authority-model.md`](operations/authority-model.md) | Exactly five target-owned procedures; stop consequential operations when principal, candidate, target or receipt is unknown. |\\n| CI controls and recurring automation | [`standards/controls.md`](standards/controls.md) and [`operations/automation-register.md`](operations/automation-register.md) | Quality workflow admission, release-graph controls, and report-only candidate boundaries; neither route grants external authority. |\\n| Verification/critical journeys/proof | [`architecture/testing-and-quality.md`](architecture/testing-and-quality.md), [`verification/critical-journeys.json`](verification/critical-journeys.json), [`evidence/releases/HGI-203-critical-journeys.json`](evidence/releases/HGI-203-critical-journeys.json), [`evidence/releases/HGI-203-local.json`](evidence/releases/HGI-203-local.json), and [`documentation-audit/HGI-203-validation.json`](documentation-audit/HGI-203-validation.json) | The current inventory owns evolving journeys. Accepted HGI-203 retains the exact historical five-journey snapshot and bounded local proof that its immutable packet observed; HGI-204 validates both epochs without attributing current changes to the old attempt. Raw logs and secrets are never durable proof. |\\n| Harness foundation and requalification | [`verification/repository-harness-profile.json`](verification/repository-harness-profile.json), [`documentation-audit/harness-foundation/accepted-findings.json`](documentation-audit/harness-foundation/accepted-findings.json), [`verification/harness-epochs.md`](verification/harness-epochs.md), and [`verification/effectiveness.md`](verification/effectiveness.md) | The TaxKit profile, accepted HE crosswalk, content-addressed skill receipt and focused gate own the implemented baseline. Last accepted epoch `HFI-004-2026-07-24` qualifies saved candidate `7c8a96e`; HGI-206 remains previous history. The active clean-slate plan owns pending qualification of today's graph. Neither saved epoch establishes current-checkout or external state. |\\n| References | [`references/README.md`](references/README.md) | Revalidate mutable external guidance. |\\n| Audit/accounting | [`documentation-audit/README.md`](documentation-audit/README.md) | Dated evidence, not policy. |\\nPreparation only; next material rate slice requires actual owning tests and review.\\n\\nPolicy owner: add a calculator request admission service and a branded, redacted/non-serialised trusted connection key in request Context. Only calculate takes a rate unit; each RPC batch member independently calls this owner. Metadata consumes zero. Local SDK/engine stay unchanged. The native application composes admission and the existing bounded calculator service once. The provider adapter decodes native success immediately, sanitises native failure and exposes only a closed named Effect; preserve native receiver. Do not add a generic callback/client escape.\\n\\nIngress: API public fetch captures a checked Cloudflare edge connection identity. Website captures its original edge connection identity before forwarding. The Website private transport calls one binding-only calculatorRequest(Request, encoded checked key) operation restricted to closed /rpc JSON. No caller-supplied HTTP forwarded-key header is trusted. Original peer trust, same/cross-zone behaviours, shared-network limitations and absent/invalid identity failures need explicit owned checks. Local synthetic edge identity is fixture authority, not a production fallback. No new analytics identity, persistent cookie or unnecessary credential.\\n\\nPrivate method: installed Alchemy bridge separately built and tested outside passes native request/response body and single counter, but transferred Request does not receive caller abort in the tested path. Do not claim remote cancellation. Return buffered closed JSON and retain the five-second application work/cleanup budget, complete ten-second client response deadline and local caller cancellation. Actual built application tests must qualify the eventual change.\\n\\nFailures: one calculator-owned rate-limit Schema shared with HTTP/RPC has fixed safe code, message and manual retry guidance. HTTP 429 declares Retry-After: 60; individual RPC errors retain checked per-member framing. Native rate-provider or identity failure is fixed safe checked unavailable, never unlimited fallback. Protocol revision/exhaustive callers/client unions and OpenAPI snapshots change through their owners. Current body/response/time/capacity failures remain intact.\\n\\nNative configuration: desired account/stage namespace is checked, collision-resistant and separated from provider reservation/readback. Local fixture namespace is not a Production choice. Native limiter is per location, permissive and eventually consistent; exact sequential local counter tests do not establish global precision. Provider plan/apply remain unauthorised.\\n\\nRequired direct observations: public + private + batch calculate units share counter; metadata budget-free; other key independent; no generic forwarded-header bypass; malformed binding/native reply yields safe failure; original body limits, five-second work/cleanup, eight places, ten-second complete-response and browser interruption remain; no rate key/facts/path/private errors in response, logs, traces, events or URL; actual generated clients see checked rate outcome without automatic retries. Original valid reports/tax/source cases unchanged before exhaustion. Run source/consumer/built journeys before full graph.\\n7:  \\\"authority\\\": \\\"Cooper explicitly authorised implementation, reviewable commits and draft PRs on 2026-10-04. No merge, deploy or publication; provider-plan approval remains separate.\\\",\\n11:    \\\"One primary owner integrates and accepts whole slices; agent or test counts do not establish proof.\\\",\\n12:    \\\"Every required owning document, README, rule, export, generated source, skill and runbook changes within the affected slice.\\\",\\n31:      \\\"Path-evidenced documentation, README, lint, skill, export, generated, CI and operational impact decisions.\\\",\\n34:      \\\"Local, Preview, provider indexing, DNS/TLS, Production and publication are separate proof boundaries.\\\"\\n52:        \\\"CSF-T004\\\"\\n67:        \\\"CSF-T004\\\",\\n113:      \\\"surface\\\": \\\"Semantic documentation, READMEs, generated/public status, runbooks and journeys\\\",\\n132:        \\\"CSF-T004\\\",\\n152:        \\\"CSF-T004\\\",\\n174:      \\\"surface\\\": \\\"New tax rates/years, accounts, persisted figures, paid features and continuous agents\\\",\\n194:        \\\"Confirm the exact branch/source and incorporate the completed Alchemy/Doppler work without overwriting another chat's changes.\\\",\\n203:      \\\"implementationPrompt\\\": \\\"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\\\",\\n227:        \\\"Other work is integrated or explicitly outside the write scope; cloud ownership is not inferred from local Git.\\\",\\n253:        \\\"Qualify the proposed exact Scheduler peer-metadata correction, or use a newer upstream fix. Preserve valid tax outputs; update package exports/types/imports and versioning consequences deliberately.\\\",\\n255:        \\\"Extend actual-command positive/negative fixtures under moved paths; assert admitted file counts, exit codes and expected rules. Prove removing/disabling required rules or broadening exact assignment/method exceptions fails the verifier. Refresh Turbo read/input/cache ownership, Knip inventories and CI commands; keep explicit generated/vendor exclusions.\\\",\\n256:        \\\"Qualify canonical rejection of let/var, assignments/writes/delete/updates, loops, native array traversal including forEach and mutators/constructors, transient Effect collection modes, switch and manual tag checks. Use existing restrictions and focused corrections for Object/Reflect writes, mutable class/contract values, WeakMap/WeakSet and demonstrated destructured/local aliases. Computed member access is already rejected by no-unchecked-index. Accept persistent collections, pure immutable Effect-managed state and qualified Alchemy Output operations. Preserve/qualify stronger lexical runtime callback/reference checks outside exact hosts. Review helper purpose, Schema ownership and pipe/flat-program call graphs separately; lint alone is not semantic proof.\\\",\\n265:      \\\"implementationPrompt\\\": \\\"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\\\",\\n296:        \\\"Deliberate bad fixtures fail with the expected rule in every owned path group, and documented valid adapters pass.\\\",\\n352:      \\\"goal\\\": \\\"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\\\",\\n355:        \\\"Implement the Q9-agreed native Effect RPC in packages/api/rpc with shared calculator/content Schemas, thin handlers and private generated client Layers. Use native JSON serialisation and explicitly select HTTP POST rather than the native server WebSocket default. Keep the public HTTP adapter separate and call the same named application operation.\\\",\\n359:        \\\"Explicitly disable unqualified platform log/trace collection on both calculator hosts; qualify the declared policy in native plans and actual local state. T009 separately owns safe exported native tracing and CSF-009 remains unmet until its export/privacy proof or a reviewed design change.\\\"\\n367:      \\\"implementationPrompt\\\": \\\"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\\\",\\n381:        \\\"Use the actual generated RPC client and native POST/JSON server through browser URL and private server binding. Prove expected error/hydration round-trip, bad valid-JSON reply, unrelated adapter defect, version skew, malformed envelopes/unknown tags/invalid IDs, sensitive sentinels in all native reply/log/trace paths, and abort during complete body decoding.\\\"\\n395:        \\\"A real calculator works through the separate apps; no frontend backend fallback exists.\\\",\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f","create_time":1791262069.708377}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
