{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T04:55:38.888Z","ordinal":37973,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ce2c79de-2674-428d-b6fc-c5fa2c18fdae","process_id":"50238","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1695,1740p' node_modules/alchemy/src/Cloudflare/Workers/Worker.ts; rg -n 'RpcWireShape|RpcReturn' node_modules/alchemy/src/Cloudflare/Workers/InferEnv.ts | head -18; sed -n '677,700p' node_modules/effect/src/rpc/RpcServer.ts; cat packages/infrastructure/package.json | tail -34"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1695,1740p' node_modules/alchemy/src/Cloudflare/Workers/Worker.ts","name":"Worker.ts","path":"node_modules/alchemy/src/Cloudflare/Workers/Worker.ts"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'RpcWireShape|RpcReturn' node_modules/alchemy/src/Cloudflare/Workers/InferEnv.ts","query":"RpcWireShape|RpcReturn","path":"InferEnv.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '677,700p' node_modules/effect/src/rpc/RpcServer.ts","name":"RpcServer.ts","path":"node_modules/effect/src/rpc/RpcServer.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"cat packages/infrastructure/package.json","name":"package.json","path":"packages/infrastructure/package.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":" * define the Worker class separately from its `.make()` call. The\n * class is a lightweight identifier; `.make()` provides the runtime\n * implementation as an `export default`. Rolldown treats `.make()`\n * as pure, so any Worker that imports the class to bind it will not\n * pull in the `.make()` dependencies — the bundler tree-shakes\n * them away entirely.\n *\n * The class and `.make()` can live in the same file. This is the\n * same pattern used by `Container` and `DurableObject`,\n * and is recommended for any cross-Worker or cross-DO bindings.\n *\n * **Example:** Worker Layer (class + .make() in one file)\n * ```typescript\n * // src/WorkerB.ts — the tag carries the name + RPC shape; props live\n * // on `.make()`.\n * export class WorkerB extends Cloudflare.Worker<\n *   WorkerB,\n *   { greet: (name: string) => Effect.Effect<string> }\n * >()(\"WorkerB\") {}\n *\n * export default WorkerB.make(\n *   { main: import.meta.url },\n *   Effect.gen(function* () {\n *     // Construction: bind resources\n *     const kv = yield* Cloudflare.KV.ReadWriteNamespace(MyKV);\n *\n *     return {\n *       // Runtime: use them\n *       greet: (name: string) =>\n *         Effect.gen(function* () {\n *           yield* kv.put(\"last-greeted\", name);\n *           return `Hello ${name}`;\n *         }),\n *     };\n *   }),\n * );\n * ```\n *\n * **Example:** Binding a Worker Layer from another Worker\n * ```typescript\n * // src/WorkerA.ts — imports WorkerB; bundler tree-shakes .make()\n * import WorkerB from \"./WorkerB.ts\";\n *\n * export default class WorkerA extends Cloudflare.Worker<WorkerA>()(\n *   \"WorkerA\",\n *   { main: import.meta.url },\n93:                  ? RpcWireShape<Shape> & Service\n179:export type RpcWireShape<Shape> = {\n    schemas: Schemas,\n    effect: Effect.Effect<unknown, Schema.SchemaError>,\n    tag: \"Chunk\" | \"Exit\"\n  ) => {\n    const collector = schemas.collector\n    // The schema encoders evaluate eagerly, so an encode that needs no\n    // services is already a resolved success and can skip the effect wrappers.\n    const write = Exit.isExit(effect) && Exit.isSuccess(effect)\n      ? send(client.id, responseEnvelope(requestId, tag, effect.value), collector && collector.clearUnsafe())\n      : Effect.flatMap(\n        Effect.provideContext(\n          collector ? Effect.provideService(effect, Transferable.Collector, collector) : effect,\n          schemas.context\n        ),\n        (value) => send(client.id, responseEnvelope(requestId, tag, value), collector && collector.clearUnsafe())\n      )\n    return Effect.catchCause(write, (cause) => {\n      client.schemas.delete(requestId)\n      const defect = Cause.squash(Cause.map(cause, (e) => SchemaIssue.defaultFormatter(e.issue)))\n      return Effect.andThen(\n        sendRequestDefect(client, requestId, schemas.encodeDefect, defect),\n        server.write(client.id, { _tag: \"Interrupt\", requestId, interruptors: [] })\n      )\n    })\n    \"./website\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/cloudflare/website.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./src/cloudflare/website.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/cloudflare/website.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./apps-stack\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/apps-stack.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./src/apps-stack.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/apps-stack.ts\"\n    },\n    \"./apps-secrets\": {\n      \"source\": \"./src/apps-secrets.boundary.ts\",\n      \"types\": \"./src/apps-secrets.boundary.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./src/apps-secrets.boundary.ts\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"check-types\": \"tsc --noEmit\",\n    \"test\": \"bun --bun vitest run\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"alchemy\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"api\": \"workspace:*\",\n    \"effect\": \"catalog:\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@effect/platform-bun\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"@effect/vitest\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"@types/bun\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"typescript\": \"catalog:\",\n    \"vitest\": \"catalog:\"\n  }\n}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":" * define the Worker class separately from its `.make()` call. The\n * class is a lightweight identifier; `.make()` provides the runtime\n * implementation as an `export default`. Rolldown treats `.make()`\n * as pure, so any Worker that imports the class to bind it will not\n * pull in the `.make()` dependencies — the bundler tree-shakes\n * them away entirely.\n *\n * The class and `.make()` can live in the same file. This is the\n * same pattern used by `Container` and `DurableObject`,\n * and is recommended for any cross-Worker or cross