{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T04:56:00.377Z","ordinal":37981,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac47f58485887d099eb5fc927ae55a8","status":"completed","call_id":"call_1KZtDChSKytBnHgUpDmVXo6n","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 - <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\np=Path('/private/tmp/dev75-rate-implementation-outline.md');s=p.read_text();s+='\\\\nImplementation call graph and file plan: calculator schemas own checked rate-limited/unavailable errors and redacted branded canonical IP identity; a named admission service has live native and focused test Layers. Hosted PublicCalculatorService rate wrapper runs admit then calculate, underneath existing PublicCalculatorServiceBounded so admission/work/cleanup share its five-second budget and eight-place pool. All metadata delegates directly and consumes zero units. HTTP declares 429 plus Retry-After 60 and safe unavailable; RPC expected union uses the same calculator-owned errors, with an explicit revision update and exhaustive client/page callers. Native API instance returns fetch and binding-only calculatorRequest(Request, encoded trusted key); both construct request Context once and share the same service/limiter. The private method keeps only /rpc POST and buffers its closed bounded JSON reply. No HTTP forwarded-key header route is introduced. Website canonical native binding type derives from API Worker RPC shape through Alchemy InferEnv/GetBindingType, rather than mirroring native Fetcher methods. Live/config/exports/generated env/test/readme owners change together.\\\\n\\\\nMetadata without identity continues through existing private fetch; calculate with missing identity safely fails, never bypasses admission. Website capture supplies its original checked request Context before its named private client. Provider limiter failure/unknown reply maps to a fixed checked unavailable error. Keep safe host telemetry on both native fetch/private methods and body/response/lifetime negative tests, including aborted caller not claiming transferred remote cancellation.\\\\n';p.write_text(s)\\nPY\",max_output_tokens:300}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"tail -6 tmp/release-readiness/verification-stdout-kPT3Pm/26ad69dacb87.log\",max_output_tokens:700}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f","create_time":1791262539.451792}}}
