{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T04:58:07.876Z","ordinal":38017,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac47fd9769887d08978c0125f15862d","status":"completed","call_id":"call_8HZqWPCXrDwIuDlQl4qIf3M2","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat > /private/tmp/dev75-domain-closeout-pr-body.md <<'EOF'\\n`CalculationError.cause` now uses the canonical nested Option type and a missing-key default while retaining the four original encoded forms: missing, explicit undefined, null and opaque value. Calculator catalogue entries expose their checked `calculate` continuation; the unused generic `program` field is removed, while rule-owned programs remain available.\\n\\nCore and genuine installed-package checks cover the original keys, bytes and hashes, constructor defaults, and removal of the unused capability. Owning READMEs, calculator/API architecture, public error guidance and four major package Changesets plus a content patch are updated together. Tax algorithms, saved results, source artifacts and OpenAPI stay unchanged.\\n\\nValidation: pending final local graph readback. Two deliberate removals fail at the owning Core test and genuine installed-consumer compiler. This draft follows #151. T004 remains active for trusted native rate identity/limits; DEV-76–81 and the unresolved Medicare decision remain separate work. No merge, publication, deployment or provider operation is included.\\nEOF\",max_output_tokens:300}));\ntext(await tools.write_stdin({session_id:90043,chars:\"\",yield_time_ms:1000,max_output_tokens:300}));\ntext(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh pr view 151 --json state,isDraft,headRefOid,statusCheckRollup\",max_output_tokens:1000}));\ntext(await tools.clock__curr_time({}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a10e2a-6616-7a42-8b17-50e4af22487f","create_time":1791262662.569371}}}
